<p data-start=3D"66" data-end=3D"276" class=3D"">Ce tutoriel vous guide =C3=
=A0 travers les <strong data-start=3D"103" data-end=3D"140">composants fond=
amentaux de Docker</strong>, du niveau d=C3=A9butant =C3=A0 expert. Vous ap=
prendrez comment ces =C3=A9l=C3=A9ments interagissent pour cr=C3=A9er une p=
lateforme robuste de conteneurisation.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"278" data-end=3D"281" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"283" data-end=3D"329" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"28=
6" data-end=3D"327">1. Introduction aux composants Docker</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"331" data-end=3D"538" class=3D"">Docker est construit sur =
une architecture modulaire avec plusieurs composants qui facilitent la cr=
=C3=A9ation, le d=C3=A9ploiement et la gestion des conteneurs. Ces composan=
ts se r=C3=A9partissent en plusieurs cat=C3=A9gories :</p>
<ol data-start=3D"540" data-end=3D"774">
<li data-start=3D"540" data-end=3D"579" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"543" data-end=3D"579" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"543=
" data-end=3D"579">Le moteur Docker (Docker Engine)</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"580" data-end=3D"643" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"583" data-end=3D"643" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"583=
" data-end=3D"643">Les objets Docker (Images, Conteneurs, Volumes, R=C3=A9s=
eaux)</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"644" data-end=3D"713" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"647" data-end=3D"713" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"647=
" data-end=3D"713">Les services Docker (Docker Compose, Docker Swarm, Kuber=
netes)</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"714" data-end=3D"774" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"717" data-end=3D"774" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"717=
" data-end=3D"774">Les registres d=E2=80=99images (Docker Hub, registres pr=
iv=C3=A9s)</strong></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start=3D"776" data-end=3D"845" class=3D"">Nous allons examiner en d=
=C3=A9tail chacun de ces composants et leur r=C3=B4le.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"847" data-end=3D"850" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"852" data-end=3D"897" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"85=
5" data-end=3D"895">2. Docker Engine : Le c=C5=93ur de Docker</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"899" data-end=3D"949" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"90=
3" data-end=3D"947">2.1. D=C3=A9finition et r=C3=B4le de Docker Engine</str=
ong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"950" data-end=3D"1081" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=3D=
"953" data-end=3D"970">Docker Engine</strong> est le logiciel principal qui=
 permet l=E2=80=99ex=C3=A9cution des conteneurs. Il est compos=C3=A9 de plu=
sieurs sous-composants :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1083" data-end=3D"1471">
<li data-start=3D"1083" data-end=3D"1231" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1085" data-end=3D"1231" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
085" data-end=3D"1117">Le daemon Docker (<code data-start=3D"1105" data-end=
=3D"1114">dockerd</code>)</strong> : un processus qui g=C3=A8re les objets =
Docker (conteneurs, images, volumes, r=C3=A9seaux) et communique avec l=E2=
=80=99API Docker.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1232" data-end=3D"1336" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1234" data-end=3D"1336" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
234" data-end=3D"1248">L'API REST</strong> : permet aux utilisateurs et aux=
 outils d=E2=80=99interagir avec Docker via des commandes HTTP.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1337" data-end=3D"1471" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1339" data-end=3D"1471" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
339" data-end=3D"1367">La CLI Docker (<code data-start=3D"1356" data-end=3D=
"1364">docker</code>)</strong> : une interface en ligne de commande qui per=
met de g=C3=A9rer Docker en interagissant avec le daemon Docker.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"1473" data-end=3D"1519" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1477" data-end=3D"1517">2.2. Fonctionnement du moteur Docker</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1520" data-end=3D"1596" class=3D"">Lorsqu=E2=80=99un utili=
sateur ex=C3=A9cute une commande Docker, voici ce qui se passe :</p>
<ol data-start=3D"1598" data-end=3D"1917">
<li data-start=3D"1598" data-end=3D"1658" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1601" data-end=3D"1658" class=3D"">La CLI <strong data-sta=
rt=3D"1608" data-end=3D"1630">envoie la commande</strong> au daemon Docker =
via l=E2=80=99API.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1659" data-end=3D"1744" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1662" data-end=3D"1744" class=3D"">Le daemon <strong data-=
start=3D"1672" data-end=3D"1697">interpr=C3=A8te et ex=C3=A9cute</strong> l=
a commande (par exemple, cr=C3=A9er un conteneur).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1745" data-end=3D"1846" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1748" data-end=3D"1846" class=3D"">Le daemon peut <strong =
data-start=3D"1763" data-end=3D"1788">t=C3=A9l=C3=A9charger une image</stro=
ng> depuis un registre si elle n=E2=80=99est pas disponible en local.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1847" data-end=3D"1917" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1850" data-end=3D"1917" class=3D"">Un conteneur est alors =
<strong data-start=3D"1873" data-end=3D"1892">cr=C3=A9=C3=A9 et ex=C3=A9cut=
=C3=A9</strong> =C3=A0 partir de cette image.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start=3D"1919" data-end=3D"1922" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"1924" data-end=3D"1953" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1927" data-end=3D"1951">3. Les objets Docker</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"1955" data-end=3D"2031" class=3D"">Docker repose sur plusi=
eurs objets essentiels pour fonctionner correctement.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"2033" data-end=3D"2065" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2037" data-end=3D"2063">3.1. Les images Docker</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2066" data-end=3D"2175" class=3D"">Une <strong data-start=
=3D"2070" data-end=3D"2079">image</strong> est un mod=C3=A8le en lecture se=
ule qui contient tout le n=C3=A9cessaire pour ex=C3=A9cuter une application=
.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"2177" data-end=3D"2216" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2182" data-end=3D"2214">3.1.1. Structure d=E2=80=99une image</strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"2217" data-end=3D"2350" class=3D"">Une image est compos=C3=
=A9e de <strong data-start=3D"2243" data-end=3D"2266">couches superpos=C3=
=A9es</strong> qui sont immuables. Ces couches permettent d=E2=80=99optimis=
er le stockage et l=E2=80=99ex=C3=A9cution :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2352" data-end=3D"2575">
<li data-start=3D"2352" data-end=3D"2444" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2354" data-end=3D"2444" class=3D"">La couche de base conti=
ent un syst=C3=A8me d=E2=80=99exploitation minimal (ex: Ubuntu, Alpine, Deb=
ian).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2445" data-end=3D"2520" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2447" data-end=3D"2520" class=3D"">Les couches interm=C3=
=A9diaires contiennent les d=C3=A9pendances et configurations.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2521" data-end=3D"2575" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2523" data-end=3D"2575" class=3D"">La derni=C3=A8re couche=
 contient l=E2=80=99application elle-m=C3=AAme.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"2577" data-end=3D"2634" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2582" data-end=3D"2632">3.1.2. Cr=C3=A9ation d=E2=80=99une image avec un Do=
ckerfile</strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"2635" data-end=3D"2735" class=3D"">Un <strong data-start=
