<h4 data-start=3D"4848" data-end=3D"4875" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4853" data-end=3D"4873">Types de r=C3=A9seaux</strong> :</h4>
<ul data-start=3D"4876" data-end=3D"5200">
<li data-start=3D"4876" data-end=3D"4983" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4878" data-end=3D"4983" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
878" data-end=3D"4888">bridge</strong> : Le type de r=C3=A9seau par d=C3=A9=
faut, permettant la communication entre les conteneurs du m=C3=AAme h=C3=B4=
te.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4984" data-end=3D"5073" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4986" data-end=3D"5073" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
986" data-end=3D"4994">host</strong> : Le conteneur partage le r=C3=A9seau =
de l=E2=80=99h=C3=B4te, ce qui =C3=A9limine l=E2=80=99isolation r=C3=A9seau=
.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5074" data-end=3D"5200" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5076" data-end=3D"5200" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
076" data-end=3D"5087">overlay</strong> : Permet la communication entre plu=
sieurs h=C3=B4tes Docker dans un environnement clusteris=C3=A9 (ex. avec Do=
cker Swarm).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"5202" data-end=3D"5224" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5206" data-end=3D"5222">4.4. Volumes</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"5226" data-end=3D"5460" class=3D"">Les volumes permettent =
de <strong data-start=3D"5252" data-end=3D"5277">conserver les donn=C3=A9es=
