<h2 data-start=3D"407" data-end=3D"444" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"41=
0" data-end=3D"444">1. Introduction =C3=A0 Docker Swarm</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"446" data-end=3D"758" class=3D"">Docker Swarm est un outil=
 d'orchestration qui vous permet de g=C3=A9rer un ensemble de machines h=C3=
=B4tes Docker (appel=C3=A9es n=C5=93uds) comme un seul cluster logique. Ce =
cluster Swarm vous permet de d=C3=A9ployer, g=C3=A9rer et mettre =C3=A0 l'=
=C3=A9chelle des services, tout en garantissant la haute disponibilit=C3=A9=
 des applications conteneuris=C3=A9es.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"760" data-end=3D"802" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"76=
4" data-end=3D"802">1.1. Concepts cl=C3=A9s de Docker Swarm</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"804" data-end=3D"1405">
<li data-start=3D"804" data-end=3D"900" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"806" data-end=3D"900" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"806=
" data-end=3D"817">Cluster</strong> : Un ensemble de n=C5=93uds Docker qui =
travaillent ensemble pour ex=C3=A9cuter des services.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"901" data-end=3D"1029" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"903" data-end=3D"1029" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"90=
3" data-end=3D"919">N=C5=93ud Manager</strong> : Responsable de la gestion =
de l'=C3=A9tat du Swarm, de la planification des t=C3=A2ches et de la gesti=
on des services.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1030" data-end=3D"1129" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1032" data-end=3D"1129" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
032" data-end=3D"1047">N=C5=93ud Worker</strong> : Ex=C3=A9cute les contene=
urs (r=C3=A9plicas des services) assign=C3=A9s par les n=C5=93uds managers.=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1130" data-end=3D"1297" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1132" data-end=3D"1297" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
132" data-end=3D"1144">Services</strong> : Une application ou un ensemble d=
